<InfoPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Modern Men's Fitness handles information: what the site collects, which third-party tools are used, how advertising works, and how to contact us."
  canonical="https://modernmensfitness.com/privacy-policy/"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="2026-11-11"
>
  <p>This policy explains what happens to information when you use modernmensfitness.com. The short version: you do not need an account, nothing you type into a calculator is sent to us, and a few third-party services collect usage information automatically.</p>

  <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
  <p>Modern Men's Fitness is run by Jordan Hoppel in Scottsdale, Arizona, United States. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:jordan@modernmensfitness.com">jordan@modernmensfitness.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>What you type into the calculators</h2>
  <p>The calculators on this site, including the 1RM, RPE, DOTS, plate, TDEE, calorie deficit, protein, macro and body fat calculators, work entirely in your web browser. The weights, measurements, ages and other numbers you enter are not sent to our servers and we do not store them.</p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically by third-party services</h2>
  <p>When you visit, the services below may collect information such as your IP address, browser and device type, the pages you view, the page that referred you, the time of your visit, your approximate location (worked out from your IP address), and identifiers stored in cookies.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics.</strong> Measures how many people visit and how pages are used. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. You can install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Meta Pixel.</strong> Meta (Facebook and Instagram) uses it to measure the results of our advertising on those platforms and to show ads to people who have visited the site. See <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta's Privacy Policy</a> and manage your ad choices in your Facebook or Instagram settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Delivers the site and protects it from abuse, and so processes visitors' IP addresses. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts.</strong> The site loads its fonts from Google, which receives your IP address when the fonts load.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choices about Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland,</strong> Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel do not load until you choose to allow them, and we rely on your consent. A banner asks you on your first visit, and rejecting is as easy as accepting.</li>
    <li><strong>Everywhere else,</strong> they load by default and you can switch them off at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Global Privacy Control.</strong> If your browser sends this signal, the Meta Pixel does not load, in any country.</li>
    <li><strong>Changing your mind.</strong> Use the Cookie settings link at the bottom of every page. Turning a tool off stops it and clears the cookies it set on this site.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We remember your choice in your browser's local storage for up to a year, so we do not ask on every visit. That choice stays in your browser and is not sent to us. We find out your country from your connection, using Cloudflare, only to decide whether to ask.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>This site may show ads served by Google AdSense or other advertising partners. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and other sites on the internet.</p>
  <p>You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>. To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small files that a site or a service stores in your browser. Google Analytics and the Meta Pixel use them for the purposes described above, and only after the choices described above. You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking cookies will not stop the site from working.</p>

  <h2>Browser extensions</h2>
  <p>Our Chrome extensions are covered by a separate policy: <a href="/privacy-policy/browser-extensions/">Browser Extension Privacy Policy</a>. They make no network requests and send us nothing.</p>

  <h2>Other sites</h2>
  <p>This site links to other websites, including <a href="https://primalpressprotocol.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">primalpressprotocol.com</a>, where the Primal Press Protocol is sold. Accounts and purchases happen there, not here, and that site has its own privacy policy. This policy does not cover other sites.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not ask you to create an account on this site.</li>
    <li>We do not collect names, email addresses or payment details on this site.</li>
    <li>We do not sell personal information that we collect.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Some advertising and analytics tools described above can be treated as "sharing" or "selling" under some US state privacy laws. The opt-out links above and your browser's privacy controls are how you limit that.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and the calculators are written for adults aged 18 and over. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to ask what information a business holds about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, and to complain to your local privacy regulator. Because we do not hold personal information ourselves, most of this information sits with the services listed above, and you can use their tools and privacy settings to exercise those rights. For anything else, email us.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top of the page will change. Material changes will be explained on this page.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:jordan@modernmensfitness.com">jordan@modernmensfitness.com</a>.</p>
</InfoPage>
